23. An electromagnetic reflector, comprising:
a body;
a first set of passages passing throughout a region of said body, arrange din a planar triangular array when penetrating a plane, and extending in parallel to each other and at a first angle of substantially 35.26° from an axis;
a second set of passages passing throughout said region of said body, arranged in said planar triangular array when penetrating said plane, and extending in parallel to each other, at said first angle from said axis, and at a second angle from said first set of passages; and
a third set of passages passing throughout said region of said body, arranged in said planar triangular array when penetrating said plane, and extending in parallel to each other, at said first angle from said axis, and at said second angle from said first and said second sets of passages;
wherein said first, second, and third sets of passages comprise a refractive index different from that of said body.
